# zig-only
# The `+` menu's child rows: a click on the curation kebab `⋯` opens
# Pin / Hide / Copy for that row. The row's hit used to be registered
# over the glyph's cell, so clicking the glyph ran the row (only the
# margin cell beside it reached the curation). This replays the
# finding's drive: alpha.zig's tab puts the `+` at column 45; the child
# menu's first row paints its kebab at column 87.
write alpha.zig "const alpha = 1;\n"
open alpha.zig
rightclick 45 1
expect screen contains "New"
click 55 2
expect screen contains "New file…"
expect screen contains "⋯"
click 87 2
expect screen contains "Pin to top"
expect screen lacks "Rename"
